\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Design envelopes of HiBER for a new material tested by a new laboratory, at a specimen size of 100 mm, by rock quality and void ratio: median (thick lines) and 5th percentile (thin lines) of the mean envelope, up to the limit of use (8 MPa).}}{28}{figure.caption.24}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Out-of-sample evaluation, leaving out each laboratory: (a) coverage of the 80\% interval by range of normal stress without site tests; and (b) mean CRPS of ln $\tau $ for held-out tests at $\sigma '_n$ $\ge $ 2 MPa with site tests at $\sigma '_n$ $\le $ 1.5 MPa (bars: 95\% bootstrap intervals over laboratories; filled: level update of the design procedure).}}{29}{figure.caption.25}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Waste rock of the example: (a) laboratory-scale envelopes by rock type with the site tests (open symbols: sets flagged by the conflict check and excluded); and (b) envelopes of placed waste rock (void ratio 0.65, rock type E 0.80; maximum particle size 1 m) by rock type and dump-average envelope. Dotted vertical lines mark the largest normal stress of the site tests.}}{30}{figure.caption.26}%
